WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.178
Hey, it's Josh.
嘿，我是乔什。

00:00:01.178 --> 00:00:04.240
Recently I appeared on a great podcast.
最近我上了一个很棒的播客。

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.460
Dinner's on me with Jesse Tyler Ferguson.
杰西·泰勒·弗格森的《客房请客》。

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:11.937
Jesse and I have known each other for a really long time.
我和杰西认识很长时间了。

00:00:11.937 --> 00:00:13.821
We have a lot in common.
我们有很多共同点。

00:00:13.821 --> 00:00:18.141
We were both on hit sitcoms at this very specific time.
我们在那个特定的时期都演过大热的情景喜剧。

00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:20.183
We're around the same age.
我们年龄相仿。

00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:30.000
But we hadn't really ever sat down and talked about the weirdness of being on a long running hit show for as long as we were.
但我们以前从未真正坐下来，好好聊聊那种长期出演大热剧集的奇妙感受，尽管我们的剧播了那么久。

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.320
We ate at a restaurant in Fort Green, Brooklyn called Evalina.
我们在布鲁克林格林堡的一家名叫埃瓦利娜的餐厅吃了饭。

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:51.560
And if you're a fan of our show, you will likely love dinners on me because he has a lot of people on that have appeared on your favorite TV shows from Lisa Kudrow to Tracy Ellis Ross to Joshua Jackson to the Edo Neal.
如果你是我们节目的粉丝，你很可能会喜欢《客房请客》，因为他请来了很多你最喜欢的电视剧里的演员，从丽莎·库卓、特雷西·埃利斯·罗斯、约书亚·杰克逊到阿迪纳·波特。

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:55.640
Now being recorded during a meal means you'll truly feel like a fly on the wall.
在一边吃饭一边录音的节目里，你会真切地感受到自己就像墙角的一只苍蝇。

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:58.932
the ambient sound of the restaurant, conversation with the server.
有餐厅的环境音，还有和服务的对话。

00:00:58.932 --> 00:01:02.175
You get to hear what people drink and how they take their coffee.
你能听到大家喝什么，以及他们怎么喝咖啡。

00:01:02.175 --> 00:01:03.722
I mean, I'm curious about that.
我是说，我对这个挺好奇的。

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:04.920
I don't know if you are.
不知道你是不是也一样。

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.945
And a good meal does let some walls down.
一顿美餐确实能让人卸下防备。

00:01:08.945 --> 00:01:16.781
And you'll hear our unguarded conversation about everything from imposter syndrome to parenting to coping after loss.
你会听到我们毫无保留的对话，从冒名顶替综合征、育儿到如何应对失去亲人的痛苦。

00:01:16.781 --> 00:01:23.879
For me, I got to talk about my evolving relationship with the character I played on how I met your mother.
对我来说，我有机会谈到我对自己在《老爸老妈浪漫史》中扮演的角色的不断变化的看法。

00:01:23.879 --> 00:01:29.840
And we got to to commiserate and share about a really crazy, wonderful time in our lives.
我们得以一起感慨并分享生命中一段非常疯狂而美妙的时光。

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:33.180
Actually, let's hear a bit of that conversation right now.
事实上，我们现在就来听听那段对话的一部分吧。

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.439
When you were starting off your career, I mean, where did you do it?
当你刚开始职业生涯的时候，我是说，你是在哪里开始的？

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:54.790
You've conquered so many different, I don't know if I've conquered the right word, but you have found success and traction and so many different facets of this industry with music and with writing and directing.
你征服了这么多不同的——我不知道“征服”是不是用得对，但你在音乐、写作和导演等这个行业的许多不同领域都取得了成功并打开了局面。

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:55.829
I love your movies, Josh.
我很喜欢你的电影，乔什。

00:01:55.829 --> 00:01:57.150
Oh, thanks, man.
哦，谢谢，老兄。

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.349
I'm really, I mean, that's mostly what I'm wanting to do.
我真的很——我是说，那基本上就是我一直想做的事。

00:02:00.349 --> 00:02:01.989
I mean, I think you're a great director.
我是说，我觉得你是个很棒的导演。

00:02:01.989 --> 00:02:04.230
You're a fantastic writer.
你是个出色的作家。

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:10.110
I'm in awe of the fact that you have not only written and directed, but also starred in those films.
我真的很佩服你，不仅自己编剧和执导，还主演了那些电影。

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.909
Yeah, I don't want to be that again.
对，我不想再那样了。

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:14.409
I was, I can only imagine that must be incredibly difficult.
我只能想象那一定极其困难。

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:16.270
Yeah.
对。

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:21.969
But when you were starting off your career, Did you have a game plan?
但当你刚开始职业生涯时，你有具体的规划吗？

00:02:21.969 --> 00:02:25.110
Or did you have an idea of what success looked like?
或者说，你对成功有一个概念吗？

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:28.189
I mean, did you know where you want to land?
我是说，你知道自己想落脚在哪里吗？

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:30.189
And was it, was what you've created?
那么，这和你创造的一切有关吗？

00:02:30.189 --> 00:02:32.069
Is this what you imagined?
这就是你想象中的样子吗？

00:02:32.069 --> 00:02:33.509
That's such a great question.
这真是个好问题。

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:40.930
You know, for years I told a story about myself that I realized was a bit of a lie.
你知道，多年来我一直对别人讲述一个关于我自己的故事，后来我意识到那其实有点谎言。

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:41.750
Okay.
好吧。

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:53.509
And the story was I wanted to be a theater actor in New York who like did the occasional law and order, but was just really committed to the theater above all things.
那个故事是，我想成为纽约的一名戏剧演员，偶尔客串一下《法律与秩序》，但无论如何最热爱的还是戏剧。

00:02:53.509 --> 00:02:58.550
And then I found these journals that I had written and like little pep talks to myself.
然后我发现了自己写过的那些日记，还有写给自己的各种小鼓励。

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:10.750
And I actually was envisioning a bigger career, bigger meaning by coastal, that involved TV and film, just more varied, I don't mean, I think the theater is like the best.
其实我当时设想的是更大的事业，“更大”的意思是兼顾东西海岸，涉足电视和电影，更多元化——我不是说，我觉得戏剧是最棒的。

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.789
But I did have my eye on the prize a little bit more than I, but I had this story.
但我确实比自己承认的更渴望成功，不过我一直编造那个故事。

00:03:15.789 --> 00:03:21.509
I think it's being from the Midwest is a very like, don't brag, don't, you know what I mean?
我想这是因为来自中西部，有一种“不要吹牛，别这样”的心态，你知道我的意思吗？

00:03:21.509 --> 00:03:29.830
I mean, I've struggled with some of that through my Columbus, Ohio, but it's got a kind of call poppy thing going.
我是说，我在哥伦布长大的经历中也为此挣扎过，这有点像“出头的椽子先烂”的文化。

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:46.039
So I think I had to, I felt like I had disguised my ambition, but I was, I remember when I did, my Broadway debut, I took over for Jason Biggs for a couple months in the graduate of Kathleen Turner, and they wanted me to come back and take over the role.
所以我当时觉得，我必须掩饰自己的野心，但我记得当我完成百老汇首秀时，我在凯瑟琳·特纳主演的《毕业生》中接替杰森·比格斯演了几个月，他们想让我回去继续演这个角色。

00:03:46.039 --> 00:03:53.759
And I told someone, I can't do this because I gotta go out to LA and get a hit TV show so I can do all the feeder I want.
我跟某个人说，我不能这么做，因为我得去洛杉矶找一部大热的电视剧，这样我以后就能演所有我想演的戏剧了。

00:03:53.759 --> 00:04:15.159
Like I had this idea, and I think some of it was from, because I went to NYU to the ground acting program, and there was this bulletin board, like the alumni board, you know, where they put up like what the alumni are doing in the world, and you know, there's reviews and good reviews are highlighted and profiles on people in all these magazines, and I would stare at it, and I was just like, am I gonna be on that board?
我当时就是这么想的，部分原因可能是因为我去了纽约大学的格拉德戏剧项目，那里有一个公告板，就是校友公告板，你知道的，上面会贴出校友们在业内的成就，还有各种评论，好评会被重点标记出来，还有各种杂志上关于人们的个人专访，我总是盯着它看，心里就在想：我会出现在那个公告板上吗？

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:21.839
Like, am I gonna be up there, you know, because I wanted my training to have be fruitful.
我会出现在那个上面吗，你知道的，因为我想让我的受训有所成果。

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:24.360
I wanted a good career.
我想要一份好的职业。

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.519
So I don't know.
所以，我不知道。

00:04:26.519 --> 00:04:31.860
I think that, yes, I wanted to be on a big TV show.
我想，是的，我确实想出演一部大型电视剧。

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.839
I wanted, I even said this to myself.
我甚至对自己说过这样的话。

00:04:33.839 --> 00:04:35.860
I want to be on a primetime show.
我想出演黄金时段的剧集。

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.000
I want to be the lead.
我想当主角。

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.800
I want it to be generationally defining.
我想让它成为定义一个时代的经典。

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.959
I want the people who created it to have never done a big hit show before because I think it's kind of lightning in a bottle.
我希望创作它的那些人之前从来没有制作过大热剧，因为我觉得那就像是奇迹般的运气。

00:04:45.959 --> 00:04:51.040
There were all these weird things that I kind of like put on my little wish list that came true.
有各种各样奇怪的事情，我把它们写进了我的小心愿单里，后来竟然都实现了。

00:04:51.040 --> 00:05:02.199
Years later, I was looking at that, and I realized I forgot to say, and I always say this now when I put it in order with the universe, I forgot to say, and I want to enjoy it.
多年后，我看着那些愿望，突然意识到我忘记说了一句话——我现在每次向宇宙许愿时都会加上这句话——我忘记说：“我还想享受这个过程。”

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:06.920
Because it took me a while to learn how to enjoy it.
因为我花了很长时间才学会如何去享受它。

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:12.920
To hear my full chat with Jesse and all its glory, please head to dinners on me.
想要收听我和杰西的完整精彩对谈，请前往《客房请客》。

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:16.240
Listen to dinners on me, wherever you listen to podcasts.
你可以在任何收听播客的地方收听《客房请客》。
